{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793463623803,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeeTm3cqgJ0o1POd","part":{"id":"prt_192c3207b001ZuPNl1wuN6f2yF","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeeTm3cqgJ0o1POd","messageID":"msg_192c31e85001DSYsZN0jJFOEHQ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"36d3bf963f92b70c042d69bdaa28837adaa75720"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793463624759,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeeTm3cqgJ0o1POd","part":{"partID":"prt_192c322ba001mOqszEDoICAp67","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeeTm3cqgJ0o1POd","messageID":"msg_192c31e85001DSYsZN0jJFOEHQ","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192c322e6728b92b07c76fa8de14a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md, lines 1-388\n1: # Backend contract v1 (Halloween TV)\n2: \n3: Source of truth for callable payloads is `backend/functions/src/contracts.ts`;\n4: exported handler composition lives in `backend/functions/src/index.ts` and\n5: `backend/functions/src/runtime.ts`. This document summarizes the wire contract\n6: for the existing TV. Machine-readable request and response examples:\n7: `test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`.\n8: \n9: ## Identity (binding rule)\n10: \n11: Requests are anonymous by default. No Firebase Auth uid, no email, no login\n12: gates on TV or generation interfaces. Every callable takes `partyId` +\n13: `deviceId` (+ `channelId`) and the server accepts them only when they match a\n14: **registered** party/device pair (`parties/{partyId}` with `status: active`,\n15: `parties/{partyId}/devices/{deviceId}` with `status: active` and matching\n16: `partyId`, plus an active channel equal to the party's `activeChannelId`).\n17: Unregistered ids → `FORBIDDEN`. Every job doc, job status and cost-log entry\n18: records `partyId`, `deviceId`/`channelId`, `manifestVersion`, `timestamp` and\n19: an idempotency key.\n20: \n21: ## Services (8)\n22: \n23: | Service | Trigger | Caller |\n24: |---|---|---|\n25: | `requestGeneration` | callable | party/device-scoped |\n26: | `runGeneration` | task queue `runGeneration` | worker only (`maxAttempts: 1`, `maxConcurrentDispatches: 1`) |\n27: | `normalizeAndStage` | internal (worker composition) | never an HTTP endpoint |\n28: | `publishManifest` | internal (worker composition) | never an HTTP endpoint |\n29: | `getCurrentManifest` | callable | party/device-scoped TV |\n30: | `getDeliveryUrls` | callable | party/device-scoped TV |\n31: | `acknowledgeDelivery` | callable | party/device-scoped TV |\n32: | `sweepExpiredMedia` | schedule `every 15 minutes` | runtime |\n33: | `requestGuestUpload` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n34: | `completeGuestUpload` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n35: | `getGuestMediaStatus` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n36: | `withdrawGuestMedia` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n37: | `createHostInvite` | callable | registered TV only |\n38: | `joinHost` | callable | phone with a valid host invite |\n39: | `listHostVideos` | callable | registered host only |\n40: | `generateHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n41: | `getHostVideoPreview` | callable | registered host only |\n42: | `deleteHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n43: \n44: Guest ingest objects live under\n45: `parties/{partyId}/guests/{deviceId}/ingest/{submissionId}/photo.jpg` with\n46: server-generated `submissionId` values only; caller-supplied paths and any\n47: cross-party/cross-device/channel substitution are rejected with `FORBIDDEN`.\n48: Firestore guest consent/media docs are callable-only (explicit deny in\n49: `firestore.rules`); Storage guest objects are callable-only (explicit deny in\n50: `storage.rules`, signed URLs bypass rules with backend validation).\n51: \n52: Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n53: `channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n54: `cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n55: `jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n56: `queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\n57: sanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n58: `deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\n59: expiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\n60: \n61: Storage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n62: (served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\n63: deny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\n64: are separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\n65: deny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\n66: `generated/{jobId}/`\n67: prefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n68: `daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n69: `sweepExpiredMedia`.\n70: \n71: ## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\n72: \n73: Supported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\n74: default when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\n75: `cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\n76: changes what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\n77: clips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\n78: manifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\n79: `core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\n80: Dart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\n81: camera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\n82: (`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\n83: clips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\n84: for count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\n85: are rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\n86: the actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\n87: rejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\n88: (`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\n89: fixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\n90: (`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\n91: `test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\n92: \n93: ## Host entry and administration\n94: \n95: The companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\n96: Scan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\n97: other partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\n98: anyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\n99: party-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\n100: reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\n101: server-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\n102: distinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\n103: Firestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\n104: \n105: - `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n106:   registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n107:   (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n108:   once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n109:   `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n110: - `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n111:   transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n112:   host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n113:   false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\n114:   guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\n115:   client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\n116:   server-side) can never grant host access.\n117: - Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \"guest\"`\n118:   server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\n119:   and never upgrades a role.\n120: - Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\n121:   `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\n122:   role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\n123:   `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\n124: \n125: ## Host seed catalog\n126: \n127: `listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\n128: `parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\n129: camera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\n130: seedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\n131: to the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\n132: budget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\n133: `hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\n134: `getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\n135: TTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\n136: `hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\n137: signs them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\n138: \n139: Deletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\n140: (deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\n141: preview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\n142: matches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\n143: ledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\n144: transactionally so deletion/withdrawal races can neither republish (the\n145: publish path rechecks the tombstone inside its transaction) nor recreate\n146: previews (deleted seeds return `NOT_FOUND` and never copy again). Guest\n147: withdrawal of a bound submission deletes retained host previews, fails the\n148: bound seed closed, and tombstones the job; the retention sweep protects live\n149: seed previews from the orphan pass and purges expired/deleted ones. Direct\n150: client access to invites, seeds, and previews remains denied (callable-only\n151: Firestore docs and Storage objects; previews are served only through signed\n152: URLs).\n153: \n154: ## Payloads\n155: \n156: - `requestGeneration { partyId, deviceId, channelId, jobId, idempotencyKey, presetId }`\n157:   — `presetId` must be `\"cheap_demo\"`; any other model/preset field is rejected\n158:   with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. The callable returns `{ jobId, state, created }`.\n159:   Same `(jobId, idempotencyKey, deviceId, channelId)` returns the existing job\n160:   (`created: false`) without enqueueing another task; reused `jobId` with\n161:   different binding → `FORBIDDEN`.\n162: - `getCurrentManifest { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` → the validated current\n163:   manifest as plain JSON, including four camera-keyed clips and a stable ISO\n164:   `createdAt` publication timestamp. It does not grant direct Firestore access;\n165:   client reads of `manifests/` remain denied by rules.\n166: - `getDeliveryUrls { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` →\n167:   `{ manifestVersion, manifestHash, clips[] }` with v4 signed read URLs capped\n168:   at the clip's own `expiresAt`. Both manifest and URL calls return only the\n169:   current version for the requested active channel. Older delivery versions\n170:   are never signed. Expired manifest/clip → `CLIP_EXPIRED`.\n171: - `acknowledgeDelivery { partyId, deviceId, channelId, manifestVersion, clipHashes }`\n172:   — `clipHashes` is a map keyed by camera ID and must carry exactly one\n173:   canonical SHA-256 hash per camera for a supported layout (1, 2, or 4\n174:   clips, first-N canonical prefix; four is the default). A first ACK must\n175:   match the unexpired current manifest exactly — same camera set, same\n176:   hashes — else `MANIFEST_MISMATCH` or\n177:   `CLIP_EXPIRED`. The accepted ACK stores the job ID and its validated\n178:   version-scoped object paths and hashes. Repeats revalidate registration and\n179:   hashes, return the same `ackId`, and retry only those stored paths even after\n180:   expiry or a newer manifest publication. A conflicting or extra hash is rejected;\n181:   objects belonging to a newer version are never purged by an older ACK.\n182: \n183: ## QR join (PIN-gated self-registration)\n184: \n185: Anonymous by default: no Firebase Auth, no names, no emails. The TV renders a\n186: session QR; the companion scans it (or pastes the same JSON) and self-registers\n187: through the `joinParty` callable, which writes the guest device doc with the\n188: Admin SDK. Direct client device writes stay denied by `firestore.rules`.\n189: \n190: - Session QR JSON (TV display, companion parse): an object with EXACTLY these\n191:   keys: `{ \"partyId\": string, \"channelId\": string }` plus OPTIONAL\n192:   `\"joinPin\"`: exactly six ASCII digits as a string (leading zeros significant,\n193:   e.g. `\"004201\"`). NEVER a deviceId, URL, or secret. Extra keys in\n194:   scanned/pasted input are ignored. The `joinPin` is intentionally carried in\n195:   the QR: it is a displayed shared admission value, not a secret, and the TV\n196:   screen is the disclosure boundary (anyone who can see the TV can read it).\n197: - Authorized set: a device admitted through `joinParty` becomes a full\n198:   party-scoped caller — it may read the current manifest, mint delivery URLs,\n199:   request generation, and ACK/purge deliveries. That breadth is the\n200:   owner-accepted consequence of anonymous admission for a co-located party\n201:   (whoever is in the room and reads the TV screen can join). The residual\n202:   risk of an unbounded admitted set is tracked as an open owner question:\n203:   per-party rate limiting/lockout and per-party guest caps/bounded\n204:   listing/operator removal are explicitly deferred pending owner protocol\n205:   decisions, not implemented controls.\n206: - `joinParty { partyId, deviceId, channelId, joinPin? }` →\n207:   `{ partyId, deviceId, channelId, role: \"guest\", status: \"active\", created }`.\n208:   `deviceId` is the phone-generated installation ID (below). `created` is true\n209:   on first registration and false on rejoin; rejoin never rewrites the stored\n210:   doc. The PIN is never echoed in the response.\n211: - `joinParty` failures use `BackendError` codes (same callable `details`\n212:   mapping as above): `FORBIDDEN` (unknown/inactive party, channel\n213:   mismatch/inactive, wrong/missing PIN when configured, deviceId colliding\n214:   with a tv-role or mismatched doc), `UNAUTHENTICATED` (missing\n215:   party/device), `INVALID_ARGUMENT` (malformed ids or PIN shape).\n216: - `listPartyDevices` (TV-only caller, unchanged gate `device.role === \"tv\"`;\n217:   guests get `FORBIDDEN`) response gains OPTIONAL `\"joinPin\"` (string when a\n218:   PIN is configured, absent otherwise). Device entries are\n219:   `{ deviceId, label?, role, status }`; `label` may be absent or empty for\n220:   self-registered guests — readers must fall back to a neutral device-based\n221:   display, never duplicate the id as label+value, never prompt for names.\n222:   Device `label` is reserved for later: omit it on create, tolerate\n223:   absent/empty on read, never require it.\n224: - PIN provisioning: `backend/functions/tools/seed_join.ts` merges `joinPin`\n225:   onto the existing party doc after validating the ACTIVE party, channel\n226:   (`== activeChannelId`), and TV registration. Explicit `--join-pin=NNNNNN`\n227:   (six digits, leading zeros preserved); preview by default, `--apply` for\n228:   writes; repeated identical provisioning is idempotent, omitting `--join-pin`\n229:   leaves an existing PIN untouched. Creates NO guest devices, collects NO\n230:   labels, uploads NO media, calls NO providers. Target guards mirror\n231:   `seed_guests.ts` (`--target=emulator|cloud`, explicit `--project` for cloud,\n232:   operator ADC, no service-account keys). Emulator trigger discovery for the\n233:   `demo-halloween-tv` project is driven by the `.env.demo-halloween-tv` file\n234:   (selects the demo project for local emulator runs; carries no secrets).\n235: - Phone installation-ID lifetime (companion): `\"p-\"` + 32 lowercase hex chars\n236:   from 128 bits of `Random.secure` entropy, persisted under one app-wide\n237:   `SharedPreferences` key and reused across launches, retries, leave, and\n238:   party changes. Corrupt stored values are replaced and re-persisted;\n239:   persistence/entropy failure surfaces retry and never proceeds unpersisted.\n240:   Reinstall/cleared data mints a new installation id and therefore a new\n241:   guest row on next join; the old row remains until operator removal\n242:   (removal tooling is an open owner question, explicitly deferred below).\n243: - Camera deferral (companion): no camera/scanner implementation ships; the\n244:   scan seam returns unavailable, and no camera permission is\n245:   declared/requested. Paste remains available without camera access. Future\n246:   work needs a permission plus validation pass before any scanning ships.\n247: - Migration away from typed guest codes: new parties use QR + PIN\n248:   self-registration. The typed-code path (`tools/guest_codes.ts`,\n249:   `tools/seed_guests.ts`, verbal dictation via `listPartyDevices`) is\n250:   unchanged and stays working — pre-seeded legacy guests (labelled device\n251:   docs) still read the current manifest via `getCurrentManifest` — but the\n252:   updated companion no longer prompts for typed codes.\n253: \n254: ## Guest upload, consent, and withdrawal\n255: \n256: Anonymous registered-device bearer model: no Firebase Auth, no login, no\n257: display name. The same party/device/channel registration gate authorizes every\n258: guest callable.\n259: \n260: - `requestGuestUpload { partyId, deviceId, channelId, consent: { accepted: true, textVersion: \"v1\", purpose: \"guest_cameo\" }, contentType: \"image/jpeg\"|\"image/png\" }`\n261:   records affirmative consent server-side (consent-text version, purpose,\n262:   timestamps, device binding, `pending_upload` status, 15-minute expiry) BEFORE\n263:   issuing a narrowly scoped short-lived signed PUT capability bound to the\n264:   server-generated object path and the content type. The capability is returned\n265:   and never persisted in Firestore or logs.\n266: - `completeGuestUpload { partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId }` verifies\n267:   the actual image bytes (JPEG/PNG magic, size within 10 MB), SHA-256, object\n268:   ownership, consent, and expiry before marking the submission `eligible` with\n269:   an immutable source hash/generation and consent revision. Repeats are\n270:   idempotent. Non-image bytes are rejected and never become eligible.\n271: - `getGuestMediaStatus { partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId }` returns\n272:   status and consent revision for the owning device only. Signed URLs are never\n273:   included.\n274: - `withdrawGuestMedia { partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId }` revokes\n275:   eligibility first (blocking new submissions and publication), deletes the\n276:   source plus attributable remaining cloud derivatives, verifies absence with\n277:   retried deletes, and retains a minimal tombstone. A PUT after withdrawal\n278:   never restores eligibility and is deleted by the `onGuestIngestFinalized`\n279:   cleanup handler. Pending uploads are protected from the orphan sweep;\n280:   abandoned/expired inputs are removed within the capped 24h input TTL.\n281: - `onGuestIngestFinalized` (storage trigger) deletes ingest objects with no\n282:   consent record, a mismatched device binding, or a withdrawn/expired status,\n283:   and leaves pending/eligible objects untouched.\n284: \n285: ## Consent-bound generation\n286: \n287: - `requestGeneration` accepts an optional `guestMediaId` bound to an eligible\n288:   guest submission (same party/device/channel, live consent, unexpired). The\n289:   binding (submission ID, immutable source hash, consent revision) is stored on\n290:   the job and rechecked at request time, at worker submission time, and\n291:   transactionally at publication. Withdrawal fails the bound job closed,\n292:   discards already-running results, and cleans staged bytes.\n293: - Guest execution plan: exactly ONE provider-generated camera slot (`CAM-01`,\n294:   carrying the validated `referenceImage` binding) plus three locally prepared\n295:   fixture slots (`CAM-02`–`CAM-04`). The four-camera manifest contract is kept\n296:   with truthful provenance: fixture slots record `fixture: true` with a null\n297:   provider task ID and null charge; they are never given fabricated provider\n298:   task IDs or charges. The single provider usage row keeps the synthetic zero\n299:   of the offline fake, explicitly not a measured charge.\n300: - Cheap-demo limits are unchanged (`wan3.0-video`, 480p, 2s, silent, 1\n301:   output); text-only behavior is preserved. The Alibaba adapter maps a present\n302:   `referenceImage` to a `reference_image { storage_ref, sha256 }` input via the\n303:   pure offline-tested `buildAlibabaSubmitBody` serializer.\n304: - Provider selection is explicit: a packaged `fixtureDirectory` never silently\n305:   forces fake mode over another configured provider. Fake selection consumes\n306:   the packaged directory; Alibaba selection resolves lazily so discovery and\n307:   local tests never require provider credentials.\n308: \n309: ## Budget guards\n310: \n311: - Max 1 generation in flight per party (`BUDGET_EXCEEDED` otherwise).\n312: - Zero automatic retries on billable calls: the task queue uses\n313:   `maxAttempts: 1` and one concurrent dispatch; each batch needs an explicit owner action\n314:   (`requestGeneration`).\n315: - Generation is disabled unless `GENERATION_ENABLED=true` is explicitly set.\n316:   The runtime uses the same generation-store/provider composition in exported\n317:   handlers and emulator tests. Queue failure marks a still-queued job failed\n318:   and releases its party budget. The fake provider is offline; Alibaba provider\n319:   construction is lazy and is not needed for module discovery or local tests.\n320: - Cost log fields: `model_id, preset_id, seconds_out, seconds_in,\n321:   credits_charged, provider_task_id, created_at, success` plus\n322:   `partyId/deviceId/channelId/manifestVersion/timestamp/idempotencyKey`.\n323: - Preset lock: `cheap_demo` only — `wan3.0-video, singapore, 480P, 2s, 16:9,\n324:   no audio, 1 output, no auto-upscale`. Contracts reject anything else; p4\n325:   enforces provider-side.\n326: \n327: ## Credentials\n328: \n329: Never in the Flutter app, manifest, public Firestore docs, or `.env.example`\n330: (placeholders only). Provider keys live server-side (Cloud Secret Manager /\n331: Functions config). No billable generation call is executed in p1; emulator\n332: seeding uses `backend/functions/tools/seed_pilot.ts` with fixture bytes.\n333: \n334: ## Error codes\n335: \n336: `UNAUTHENTICATED` (missing party/device) · `FORBIDDEN` (unregistered/inactive\n337: party-device-channel or idempotency mismatch) · `MANIFEST_MISMATCH` ·\n338: `CLIP_EXPIRED` · `PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE` · `BUDGET_EXCEEDED` ·\n339: `INVALID_ARGUMENT` · `NOT_FOUND` · `INTERNAL`.\n340: \n341: Callable failures use Firebase `HttpsError` codes with `details: { errorCode }`.\n342: The detail preserves the backend code above; Firebase codes are respectively\n343: `unauthenticated`, `permission-denied`, `failed-precondition`,\n344: `failed-precondition`, `unavailable`, `resource-exhausted`, `invalid-argument`,\n345: `not-found`, and `internal`.\n346: \n347: ## Local verification and operator switch\n348: \n349: From `backend/functions`, `npm run build` checks the TypeScript deployment\n350: composition. `npm run test:emulator` runs Firestore and Storage emulator tests\n351: serially. These tests use the deterministic fake provider and repository MP4\n352: fixtures; they make no provider network calls. The emulator signing\n353: substitutes (deterministic capability strings) are not equivalent to cloud v4\n354: signed URLs / IAM signing; they only prove per-submission scoping without\n355: persistence. Keep generation disabled during\n356: module discovery and normal local development. A deliberate runtime opt-in is\n357: `GENERATION_ENABLED=true`; selecting the fake provider with\n358: `VIDEO_GENERATION_PROVIDER=fake` remains offline. Deployment and provider\n359: credential setup are outside this contract change.\n360: \n361: ## Tests\n362: \n363: `contracts.test.ts` (payload validation + 1/2/4 prefix checks + host parser\n364: shape checks + in-flight/idempotency/error paths),\n365: `backend_contract_fixture.test.ts` (shared JSON fixture through parsing, hashing,\n366: callable service paths, delivery, and ACK, plus the `cctv_counts_v1` count\n367: vectors with legacy four-camera hash preservation), `runtime.test.ts` (disabled default,\n368: queue failure, and fake four-camera generation through handler composition),\n369: `host_join.test.ts` (TV-only invite minting, transactional host redemption,\n370: idempotent retry, replay/expiry/PIN/role-forgery denial, guest-only legacy\n371: join), `host_media.test.ts` (seed catalog queue/idempotency, preview\n372: materialization and ACK survival, deletion outcomes and race protection),\n373: `host_admin_e2e.test.ts` (exported callable coverage and the full host flow\n374: through real runtime generation with the fixture-backed provider and emulator\n375: storage), `security_rules.test.ts` (party/device-scoped registration reads, denied client\n376: registration writes, denied device listing and party/PIN reads, denied manifest\n377: reads, denied host-invite/seed direct access), `seed_join.test.ts` (PIN provisioning preview/apply/idempotency/omit and\n378: refusal paths against the emulator), `qr_join_e2e.test.ts` (PIN-gated join,\n379: rejoin, TV listing, and legacy manifest read through the real exported Functions\n380: emulator endpoints with no auth), `delivery.test.ts` (URL scoping, manifest callable, ACK hash\n381: checks incl. 1/2/4 exact-match and extra-hash rejection, bounded retry purge), and `retention.test.ts` (TTL transitions, orphan\n382: sweeper, host preview protection/expiry). Guest flows are covered by `guest_upload.test.ts` (consent refusal,\n383: completion, scoping, withdrawal, deletion retry, TTL/orphan protection,\n384: generation refusal, retained host-preview cleanup), `guest_upload_e2e.test.ts` (real-bytes endpoint lifecycle),\n385: `guest_media_generation.test.ts` (one provider camera plus three fixture slots,\n386: truthful usage, withdrawal races), and `alibaba.test.ts` (offline guest-image\n387: serialization fixture, zero network). Emulator-backed cases skip when `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST` is unset;\n388: run `npm run test:emulator` (project `demo-halloween-tv`) for the full suite.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md, lines 1-388\n1: # Backend contract v1 (Halloween TV)\n2: \n3: Source of truth for callable payloads is `backend/functions/src/contracts.ts`;\n4: exported handler composition lives in `backend/functions/src/index.ts` and\n5: `backend/functions/src/runtime.ts`. This document summarizes the wire contract\n6: for the existing TV. Machine-readable request and response examples:\n7: `test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`.\n8: \n9: ## Identity (binding rule)\n10: \n11: Requests are anonymous by default. No Firebase Auth uid, no email, no login\n12: gates on TV or generation interfaces. Every callable takes `partyId` +\n13: `deviceId` (+ `channelId`) and the server accepts them only when they match a\n14: **registered** party/device pair (`parties/{partyId}` with `status: active`,\n15: `parties/{partyId}/devices/{deviceId}` with `status: active` and matching\n16: `partyId`, plus an active channel equal to the party's `activeChannelId`).\n17: Unregistered ids → `FORBIDDEN`. Every job doc, job status and cost-log entry\n18: records `partyId`, `deviceId`/`channelId`, `manifestVersion`, `timestamp` and\n19: an idempotency key.\n20: \n21: ## Services (8)\n22: \n23: | Service | Trigger | Caller |\n24: |---|---|---|\n25: | `requestGeneration` | callable | party/device-scoped |\n26: | `runGeneration` | task queue `runGeneration` | worker only (`maxAttempts: 1`, `maxConcurrentDispatches: 1`) |\n27: | `normalizeAndStage` | internal (worker composition) | never an HTTP endpoint |\n28: | `publishManifest` | internal (worker composition) | never an HTTP endpoint |\n29: | `getCurrentManifest` | callable | party/device-scoped TV |\n30: | `getDeliveryUrls` | callable | party/device-scoped TV |\n31: | `acknowledgeDelivery` | callable | party/device-scoped TV |\n32: | `sweepExpiredMedia` | schedule `every 15 minutes` | runtime |\n33: | `requestGuestUpload` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n34: | `completeGuestUpload` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n35: | `getGuestMediaStatus` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n36: | `withdrawGuestMedia` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n37: | `createHostInvite` | callable | registered TV only |\n38: | `joinHost` | callable | phone with a valid host invite |\n39: | `listHostVideos` | callable | registered host only |\n40: | `generateHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n41: | `getHostVideoPreview` | callable | registered host only |\n42: | `deleteHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n43: \n44: Guest ingest objects live under\n45: `parties/{partyId}/guests/{deviceId}/ingest/{submissionId}/photo.jpg` with\n46: server-generated `submissionId` values only; caller-supplied paths and any\n47: cross-party/cross-device/channel substitution are rejected with `FORBIDDEN`.\n48: Firestore guest consent/media docs are callable-only (explicit deny in\n49: `firestore.rules`); Storage guest objects are callable-only (explicit deny in\n50: `storage.rules`, signed URLs bypass rules with backend validation).\n51: \n52: Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n53: `channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n54: `cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n55: `jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n56: `queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\n57: sanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n58: `deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\n59: expiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\n60: \n61: Storage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n62: (served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\n63: deny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\n64: are separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\n65: deny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\n66: `generated/{jobId}/`\n67: prefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n68: `daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n69: `sweepExpiredMedia`.\n70: \n71: ## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\n72: \n73: Supported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\n74: default when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\n75: `cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\n76: changes what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\n77: clips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\n78: manifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\n79: `core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\n80: Dart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\n81: camera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\n82: (`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\n83: clips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\n84: for count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\n85: are rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\n86: the actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\n87: rejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\n88: (`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\n89: fixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\n90: (`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\n91: `test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\n92: \n93: ## Host entry and administration\n94: \n95: The companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\n96: Scan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\n97: other partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\n98: anyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\n99: party-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\n100: reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\n101: server-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\n102: distinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\n103: Firestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\n104: \n105: - `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n106:   registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n107:   (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n108:   once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n109:   `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n110: - `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n111:   transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n112:   host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n113:   false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\n114:   guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\n115:   client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\n116:   server-side) can never grant host access.\n117: - Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \"guest\"`\n118:   server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\n119:   and never upgrades a role.\n120: - Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\n121:   `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\n122:   role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\n123:   `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\n124: \n125: ## Host seed catalog\n126: \n127: `listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\n128: `parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\n129: camera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\n130: seedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\n131: to the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\n132: budget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\n133: `hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\n134: `getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\n135: TTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\n136: `hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\n137: signs them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\n138: \n139: Deletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\n140: (deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\n141: preview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\n142: matches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\n143: ledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\n144: transactionally so deletion/withdrawal races can neither republish (the\n145: publish path rechecks the tombstone inside its transaction) nor recreate\n146: previews (deleted seeds return `NOT_FOUND` and never copy again). Guest\n147: withdrawal of a bound submission deletes retained host previews, fails the\n148: bound seed closed, and tombstones the job; the retention sweep protects live\n149: seed previews from the orphan pass and purges expired/deleted ones. Direct\n150: client access to invites, seeds, and previews remains denied (callable-only\n151: Firestore docs and Storage objects; previews are served only through signed\n152: URLs).\n153: \n154: ## Payloads\n155: \n156: - `requestGeneration { partyId, deviceId, channelId, jobId, idempotencyKey, presetId }`\n157:   — `presetId` must be `\"cheap_demo\"`; any other model/preset field is rejected\n158:   with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. The callable returns `{ jobId, state, created }`.\n159:   Same `(jobId, idempotencyKey, deviceId, channelId)` returns the existing job\n160:   (`created: false`) without enqueueing another task; reused `jobId` with\n161:   different binding → `FORBIDDEN`.\n162: - `getCurrentManifest { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` → the validated current\n163:   manifest as plain JSON, including four camera-keyed clips and a stable ISO\n164:   `createdAt` publication timestamp. It does not grant direct Firestore access;\n165:   client reads of `manifests/` remain denied by rules.\n166: - `getDeliveryUrls { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` →\n167:   `{ manifestVersion, manifestHash, clips[] }` with v4 signed read URLs capped\n168:   at the clip's own `expiresAt`. Both manifest and URL calls return only the\n169:   current version for the requested active channel. Older delivery versions\n170:   are never signed. Expired manifest/clip → `CLIP_EXPIRED`.\n171: - `acknowledgeDelivery { partyId, deviceId, channelId, manifestVersion, clipHashes }`\n172:   — `clipHashes` is a map keyed by camera ID and must carry exactly one\n173:   canonical SHA-256 hash per camera for a supported layout (1, 2, or 4\n174:   clips, first-N canonical prefix; four is the default). A first ACK must\n175:   match the unexpired current manifest exactly — same camera set, same\n176:   hashes — else `MANIFEST_MISMATCH` or\n177:   `CLIP_EXPIRED`. The accepted ACK stores the job ID and its validated\n178:   version-scoped object paths and hashes. Repeats revalidate registration and\n179:   hashes, return the same `ackId`, and retry only those stored paths even after\n180:   expiry or a newer manifest publication. A conflicting or extra hash is rejected;\n181:   objects belonging to a newer version are never purged by an older ACK.\n182: \n183: ## QR join (PIN-gated self-registration)\n184: \n185: Anonymous by default: no Firebase Auth, no names, no emails. The TV renders a\n186: session QR; the companion scans it (or pastes the same JSON) and self-registers\n187: through the `joinParty` callable, which writes the guest device doc with the\n188: Admin SDK. Direct client device writes stay denied by `firestore.rules`.\n189: \n190: - Session QR JSON (TV display, companion parse): an object with EXACTLY these\n191:   keys: `{ \"partyId\": string, \"channelId\": string }` plus OPTIONAL\n192:   `\"joinPin\"`: exactly six ASCII digits as a string (leading zeros significant,\n193:   e.g. `\"004201\"`). NEVER a deviceId, URL, or secret. Extra keys in\n194:   scanned/pasted input are ignored. The `joinPin` is intentionally carried in\n195:   the QR: it is a displayed shared admission value, not a secret, and the TV\n196:   screen is the disclosure boundary (anyone who can see the TV can read it).\n197: - Authorized set: a device admitted through `joinParty` becomes a full\n198:   party-scoped caller — it may read the current manifest, mint delivery URLs,\n199:   request generation, and ACK/purge deliveries. That breadth is the\n200:   owner-accepted consequence of anonymous admission for a co-located party\n201:   (whoever is in the room and reads the TV screen can join). The residual\n202:   risk of an unbounded admitted set is tracked as an open owner question:\n203:   per-party rate limiting/lockout and per-party guest caps/bounded\n204:   listing/operator removal are explicitly deferred pending owner protocol\n205:   decisions, not implemented controls.\n206: - `joinParty { partyId, deviceId, channelId, joinPin? }` →\n207:   `{ partyId, deviceId, channelId, role: \"guest\", status: \"active\", created }`.\n208:   `deviceId` is the phone-generated installation ID (below). `created` is true\n209:   on first registration and false on rejoin; rejoin never rewrites the stored\n210:   doc. The PIN is never echoed in the response.\n211: - `joinParty` failures use `BackendError` codes (same callable `details`\n212:   mapping as above): `FORBIDDEN` (unknown/inactive party, channel\n213:   mismatch/inactive, wrong/missing PIN when configured, deviceId colliding\n214:   with a tv-role or mismatched doc), `UNAUTHENTICATED` (missing\n215:   party/device), `INVALID_ARGUMENT` (malformed ids or PIN shape).\n216: - `listPartyDevices` (TV-only caller, unchanged gate `device.role === \"tv\"`;\n217:   guests get `FORBIDDEN`) response gains OPTIONAL `\"joinPin\"` (string when a\n218:   PIN is configured, absent otherwise). Device entries are\n219:   `{ deviceId, label?, role, status }`; `label` may be absent or empty for\n220:   self-registered guests — readers must fall back to a neutral device-based\n221:   display, never duplicate the id as label+value, never prompt for names.\n222:   Device `label` is reserved for later: omit it on create, tolerate\n223:   absent/empty on read, never require it.\n224: - PIN provisioning: `backend/functions/tools/seed_join.ts` merges `joinPin`\n225:   onto the existing party doc after validating the ACTIVE party, channel\n226:   (`== activeChannelId`), and TV registration. Explicit `--join-pin=NNNNNN`\n227:   (six digits, leading zeros preserved); preview by default, `--apply` for\n228:   writes; repeated identical provisioning is idempotent, omitting `--join-pin`\n229:   leaves an existing PIN untouched. Creates NO guest devices, collects NO\n230:   labels, uploads NO media, calls NO providers. Target guards mirror\n231:   `seed_guests.ts` (`--target=emulator|cloud`, explicit `--project` for cloud,\n232:   operator ADC, no service-account keys). Emulator trigger discovery for the\n233:   `demo-halloween-tv` project is driven by the `.env.demo-halloween-tv` file\n234:   (selects the demo project for local emulator runs; carries no secrets).\n235: - Phone installation-ID lifetime (companion): `\"p-\"` + 32 lowercase hex chars\n236:   from 128 bits of `Random.secure` entropy, persisted under one app-wide\n237:   `SharedPreferences` key and reused across launches, retries, leave, and\n238:   party changes. Corrupt stored values are replaced and re-persisted;\n239:   persistence/entropy failure surfaces retry and never proceeds unpersisted.\n240:   Reinstall/cleared data mints a new installation id and therefore a new\n241:   guest row on next join; the old row remains until operator removal\n242:   (removal tooling is an open owner question, explicitly deferred below).\n243: - Camera deferral (companion): no camera/scanner implementation ships; the\n244:   scan seam returns unavailable, and no camera permission is\n245:   declared/requested. Paste remains available without camera access. Future\n246:   work needs a permission plus validation pass before any scanning ships.\n247: - Migration away from typed guest codes: new parties use QR + PIN\n248:   self-registration. The typed-code path (`tools/guest_codes.ts`,\n249:   `tools/seed_guests.ts`, verbal dictation via `listPartyDevices`) is\n250:   unchanged and stays working — pre-seeded legacy guests (labelled device\n251:   docs) still read the current manifest via `getCurrentManifest` — but the\n252:   updated companion no longer prompts for typed codes.\n253: \n254: ## Guest upload, consent, and withdrawal\n255: \n256: Anonymous registered-device bearer model: no Firebase Auth, no login, no\n257: display name. The same party/device/channel registration gate authorizes every\n258: guest callable.\n259: \n260: - `requestGuestUpload { partyId, deviceId, channelId, consent: { accepted: true, textVersion: \"v1\", purpose: \"guest_cameo\" }, contentType: \"image/jpeg\"|\"image/png\" }`\n261:   records affirmative consent server-side (consent-text version, purpose,\n262:   timestamps, device binding, `pending_upload` status, 15-minute expiry) BEFORE\n263:   issuing a narrowly scoped short-lived signed PUT capability bound to the\n264:   server-generated object path and the content type. The capability is returned\n265:   and never persisted in Firestore or logs.\n266: - `completeGuestUpload { partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId }` verifies\n267:   the actual image bytes (JPEG/PNG magic, size within 10 MB), SHA-256, object\n268:   ownership, consent, and expiry before marking the submission `eligible` with\n269:   an immutable source hash/generation and consent revision. Repeats are\n270:   idempotent. Non-image bytes are rejected and never become eligible.\n271: - `getGuestMediaStatus { partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId }` returns\n272:   status and consent revision for the owning device only. Signed URLs are never\n273:   included.\n274: - `withdrawGuestMedia { partyId, deviceId, channelId, submissionId }` revokes\n275:   eligibility first (blocking new submissions and publication), deletes the\n276:   source plus attributable remaining cloud derivatives, verifies absence with\n277:   retried deletes, and retains a minimal tombstone. A PUT after withdrawal\n278:   never restores eligibility and is deleted by the `onGuestIngestFinalized`\n279:   cleanup handler. Pending uploads are protected from the orphan sweep;\n280:   abandoned/expired inputs are removed within the capped 24h input TTL.\n281: - `onGuestIngestFinalized` (storage trigger) deletes ingest objects with no\n282:   consent record, a mismatched device binding, or a withdrawn/expired status,\n283:   and leaves pending/eligible objects untouched.\n284: \n285: ## Consent-bound generation\n286: \n287: - `requestGeneration` accepts an optional `guestMediaId` bound to an eligible\n288:   guest submission (same party/device/channel, live consent, unexpired). The\n289:   binding (submission ID, immutable source hash, consent revision) is stored on\n290:   the job and rechecked at request time, at worker submission time, and\n291:   transactionally at publication. Withdrawal fails the bound job closed,\n292:   discards already-running results, and cleans staged bytes.\n293: - Guest execution plan: exactly ONE provider-generated camera slot (`CAM-01`,\n294:   carrying the validated `referenceImage` binding) plus three locally prepared\n295:   fixture slots (`CAM-02`–`CAM-04`). The four-camera manifest contract is kept\n296:   with truthful provenance: fixture slots record `fixture: true` with a null\n297:   provider task ID and null charge; they are never given fabricated provider\n298:   task IDs or charges. The single provider usage row keeps the synthetic zero\n299:   of the offline fake, explicitly not a measured charge.\n300: - Cheap-demo limits are unchanged (`wan3.0-video`, 480p, 2s, silent, 1\n301:   output); text-only behavior is preserved. The Alibaba adapter maps a present\n302:   `referenceImage` to a `reference_image { storage_ref, sha256 }` input via the\n303:   pure offline-tested `buildAlibabaSubmitBody` serializer.\n304: - Provider selection is explicit: a packaged `fixtureDirectory` never silently\n305:   forces fake mode over another configured provider. Fake selection consumes\n306:   the packaged directory; Alibaba selection resolves lazily so discovery and\n307:   local tests never require provider credentials.\n308: \n309: ## Budget guards\n310: \n311: - Max 1 generation in flight per party (`BUDGET_EXCEEDED` otherwise).\n312: - Zero automatic retries on billable calls: the task queue uses\n313:   `maxAttempts: 1` and one concurrent dispatch; each batch needs an explicit owner action\n314:   (`requestGeneration`).\n315: - Generation is disabled unless `GENERATION_ENABLED=true` is explicitly set.\n316:   The runtime uses the same generation-store/provider composition in exported\n317:   handlers and emulator tests. Queue failure marks a still-queued job failed\n318:   and releases its party budget. The fake provider is offline; Alibaba provider\n319:   construction is lazy and is not needed for module discovery or local tests.\n320: - Cost log fields: `model_id, preset_id, seconds_out, seconds_in,\n321:   credits_charged, provider_task_id, created_at, success` plus\n322:   `partyId/deviceId/channelId/manifestVersion/timestamp/idempotencyKey`.\n323: - Preset lock: `cheap_demo` only — `wan3.0-video, singapore, 480P, 2s, 16:9,\n324:   no audio, 1 output, no auto-upscale`. Contracts reject anything else; p4\n325:   enforces provider-side.\n326: \n327: ## Credentials\n328: \n329: Never in the Flutter app, manifest, public Firestore docs, or `.env.example`\n330: (placeholders only). Provider keys live server-side (Cloud Secret Manager /\n331: Functions config). No billable generation call is executed in p1; emulator\n332: seeding uses `backend/functions/tools/seed_pilot.ts` with fixture bytes.\n333: \n334: ## Error codes\n335: \n336: `UNAUTHENTICATED` (missing party/device) · `FORBIDDEN` (unregistered/inactive\n337: party-device-channel or idempotency mismatch) · `MANIFEST_MISMATCH` ·\n338: `CLIP_EXPIRED` · `PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE` · `BUDGET_EXCEEDED` ·\n339: `INVALID_ARGUMENT` · `NOT_FOUND` · `INTERNAL`.\n340: \n341: Callable failures use Firebase `HttpsError` codes with `details: { errorCode }`.\n342: The detail preserves the backend code above; Firebase codes are respectively\n343: `unauthenticated`, `permission-denied`, `failed-precondition`,\n344: `failed-precondition`, `unavailable`, `resource-exhausted`, `invalid-argument`,\n345: `not-found`, and `internal`.\n346: \n347: ## Local verification and operator switch\n348: \n349: From `backend/functions`, `npm run build` checks the TypeScript deployment\n350: composition. `npm run test:emulator` runs Firestore and Storage emulator tests\n351: serially. These tests use the deterministic fake provider and repository MP4\n352: fixtures; they make no provider network calls. The emulator signing\n353: substitutes (deterministic capability strings) are not equivalent to cloud v4\n354: signed URLs / IAM signing; they only prove per-submission scoping without\n355: persistence. Keep generation disabled during\n356: module discovery and normal local development. A deliberate runtime opt-in is\n357: `GENERATION_ENABLED=true`; selecting the fake provider with\n358: `VIDEO_GENERATION_PROVIDER=fake` remains offline. Deployment and provider\n359: credential setup are outside this contract change.\n360: \n361: ## Tests\n362: \n363: `contracts.test.ts` (payload validation + 1/2/4 prefix checks + host parser\n364: shape checks + in-flight/idempotency/error paths),\n365: `backend_contract_fixture.test.ts` (shared JSON fixture through parsing, hashing,\n366: callable service paths, delivery, and ACK, plus the `cctv_counts_v1` count\n367: vectors with legacy four-camera hash preservation), `runtime.test.ts` (disabled default,\n368: queue failure, and fake four-camera generation through handler composition),\n369: `host_join.test.ts` (TV-only invite minting, transactional host redemption,\n370: idempotent retry, replay/expiry/PIN/role-forgery denial, guest-only legacy\n371: join), `host_media.test.ts` (seed catalog queue/idempotency, preview\n372: materialization and ACK survival, deletion outcomes and race protection),\n373: `host_admin_e2e.test.ts` (exported callable coverage and the full host flow\n374: through real runtime generation with the fixture-backed provider and emulator\n375: storage), `security_rules.test.ts` (party/device-scoped registration reads, denied client\n376: registration writes, denied device listing and party/PIN reads, denied manifest\n377: reads, denied host-invite/seed direct access), `seed_join.test.ts` (PIN provisioning preview/apply/idempotency/omit and\n378: refusal paths against the emulator), `qr_join_e2e.test.ts` (PIN-gated join,\n379: rejoin, TV listing, and legacy manifest read through the real exported Functions\n380: emulator endpoints with no auth), `delivery.test.ts` (URL scoping, manifest callable, ACK hash\n381: checks incl. 1/2/4 exact-match and extra-hash rejection, bounded retry purge), and `retention.test.ts` (TTL transitions, orphan\n382: sweeper, host preview protection/expiry). Guest flows are covered by `guest_upload.test.ts` (consent refusal,\n383: completion, scoping, withdrawal, deletion retry, TTL/orphan protection,\n384: generation refusal, retained host-preview cleanup), `guest_upload_e2e.test.ts` (real-bytes endpoint lifecycle),\n385: `guest_media_generation.test.ts` (one provider camera plus three fixture slots,\n386: truthful usage, withdrawal races), and `alibaba.test.ts` (offline guest-image\n387: serialization fixture, zero network). Emulator-backed cases skip when `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST` is unset;\n388: run `npm run test:emulator` (project `demo-halloween-tv`) for the full suite."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192c322e6728b92b07c76fa8de14a"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793463624378,"end":1793463624759}}}}
