{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793463996010,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeeTm3cqgJ0o1POd","part":{"partID":"prt_192c8c1cd001wlzeQ1hXbWGHQe","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeeTm3cqgJ0o1POd","messageID":"msg_192c8b933001ziY4QkQZ7KwUz6","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192c8c0e574d89837b323aa1bfefa","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"error","input":{"newString":"- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n  registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n  once alongside a server-minted 6-digit `pairingCode` (displayed next to the\n  HOST QR on the TV); only the SHA-256 token hash and a salted pairing-code\n  hash are stored at `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to\n  party/channel/expiry with the same 5-minute TTL. Minting a new invite\n  supersedes older pending invites for the same party/channel. Invite docs\n  carry `expiresAt` for the Firestore TTL policy plus the retention-sweep\n  expiry pass.\n- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken, pairingCode }`\n  redeems the invite transactionally for a separate phone identity with the\n  server-assigned host role. BOTH halves are required: a wrong or missing\n  pairing code denies generically with the same error as an unknown invite\n  (no oracle). Same-device redemption retries are idempotent\n  (`created: false`); other-device replay, expiry, guest PIN reuse\n  (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), over-capacity redemption\n  (max 3 active host devices per party; further redemption is denied until a\n  host is revoked), and client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is\n  always written server-side) can never grant host access. Redemption records\n  `redeemedFromInviteId`/`redeemedAt` on the device doc.\n- `revokeHostDevice { partyId, deviceId, targetDeviceId }` (TV-only caller:\n  same registered-TV gate as `createHostInvite`) demotes a host device doc\n  (`status: \"revoked\"`) and writes a `parties/{partyId}/hostAudit` audit\n  record. A revoked host fails the registered-host gate on its next admin\n  operation.","oldString":"- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n  registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n  false`); other-device replay, expiry, guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings\n  are shape-rejected as tokens), and client-supplied role fields (ignored;\n  the role is always written server-side) can never grant host access.","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md"},"error":"Could not find oldString in /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md. It must match exactly, including whitespace and indentation.","metadata":{"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192c8c0e574d89837b323aa1bfefa"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\\n  registered device with `role: \\\"tv\\\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\\n  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\\n  once alongside a server-minted 6-digit `pairingCode` (displayed next to the\\n  HOST QR on the TV); only the SHA-256 token hash and a salted pairing-code\\n  hash are stored at `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to\\n  party/channel/expiry with the same 5-minute TTL. Minting a new invite\\n  supersedes older pending invites for the same party/channel. Invite docs\\n  carry `expiresAt` for the Firestore TTL policy plus the retention-sweep\\n  expiry pass.\\n- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken, pairingCode }`\\n  redeems the invite transactionally for a separate phone identity with the\\n  server-assigned host role. BOTH halves are required: a wrong or missing\\n  pairing code denies generically with the same error as an unknown invite\\n  (no oracle). Same-device redemption retries are idempotent\\n  (`created: false`); other-device replay, expiry, guest PIN reuse\\n  (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), over-capacity redemption\\n  (max 3 active host devices per party; further redemption is denied until a\\n  host is revoked), and client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is\\n  always written server-side) can never grant host access. Redemption records\\n  `redeemedFromInviteId`/`redeemedAt` on the device doc.\\n- `revokeHostDevice { partyId, deviceId, targetDeviceId }` (TV-only caller:\\n  same registered-TV gate as `createHostInvite`) demotes a host device doc\\n  (`status: \\\"revoked\\\"`) and writes a `parties/{partyId}/hostAudit` audit\\n  record. A revoked host fails the registered-host gate on its next admin\\n  operation.\",\"oldString\":\"- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\\n  registered device with `role: \\\"tv\\\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\\n  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\\n  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\\n  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\\n- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\\n  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\\n  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\\n  false`); other-device replay, expiry, guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings\\n  are shape-rejected as tokens), and client-supplied role fields (ignored;\\n